The installed Cursor hooks are built by agentcoop, not from this file.
They are .cursor/hooks.json in the project.
Stop: {{AGENTCOOP}} hook cursor-stop --as {{AGENT_NAME}}
Before a prompt: {{AGENTCOOP}} hook cursor-prompt --as {{AGENT_NAME}}
The default timeout is 3600 seconds. loop_limit is unlimited.
The stop hook waits until 5 seconds are left.
If this agent did anything after the hook started, it sends nothing.
No mail sends: Agent Co-op keep-awake. If you are working on anything, ignore this and keep going. Otherwise end your turn.
Mail says to handle it, mark it done, then continue. End the turn only when there is nothing else.
sessionStart cannot start a command, so the rule starts cursor-loop.
